{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the nested indexed likelihood statements `y[n, t] ~ normal(...)` with a single vectorized built-in sampling statement `y ~ normal(mu_y, sigma_y)` on the top-level protected matrix `y`. The local matrix `mu_y` is computed after all parameter priors in the model block. This preserves the original product of normal likelihood terms while satisfying SafeStan's requirement that protected data be observed exactly once with a plain top-level left-hand side and not inside loops.

The data file is unchanged.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  int<lower=1> T;
  vector[T] time;
  matrix[N, T] y;
}
parameters {
  real mu_alpha;
  real mu_beta;
  real<lower=0> sigma_alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigma_beta;
  real<lower=0> sigma_y;
  vector[N] alpha_raw;
  vector[N] beta_raw;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[N] alpha = mu_alpha + sigma_alpha * alpha_raw;
  vector[N] beta = mu_beta + sigma_beta * beta_raw;
}
model {
  mu_alpha ~ normal(50, 20);
  mu_beta ~ normal(7, 5);
  sigma_alpha ~ normal(0, 10);
  sigma_beta ~ normal(0, 5);
  sigma_y ~ normal(0, 5);
  alpha_raw ~ normal(0, 1);
  beta_raw ~ normal(0, 1);

  {
    matrix[N, T] mu_y;
    for (n in 1 : N) {
      for (t in 1 : T) {
        mu_y[n, t] = alpha[n] + beta[n] * time[t];
      }
    }
    y ~ normal(mu_y, sigma_y);
  }
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":5,"T":5,"time":[0.0,1.0,2.0,3.0,4.0],"y":[[50,58,65,72,81],[48,55,61,69,76],[52,61,68,75,83],[47,53,59,66,72],[51,59,67,73,80]]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
